From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graeme Smecher <gsmecher@t0.technology>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:12:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix internal error on force/release of whole unpacked arrays
 (#9090)

  logic [3:0] a[2], b[2];
  force a = '{default: 0};  // sliced into element forces
  release a;                // Internal Error: Whole unpacked-array
                            // force/release should have been lowered
                            // via element selections
  force a = b;              // likewise
  assign a = b;             // likewise

V3Force handles force, release, assign and deassign of an unpacked array
only by element, and relies on V3Slice to split them. V3Slice never split
a release, deassign or procedural assign, and left a force whole for a
copy between arrays of one type, with -fno-slice, or above
--fslice-element-limit. It now always splits these. Xilinx's XPM CDC
macros force and release whole arrays to model GSR.
Bug: https://github.com/verilator/verilator/issues/9090
Forwarded: https://github.com/verilator/verilator/pull/9091
Last-Update: 2026-11-08
---
